whether the own-principal no-own-key fallthrough (src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:121-123) also calls _pinned_environment_keys with unrevoked_only=True, or scope it explicitly out with a stated reason.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_opcert_trust_root falls through to `pinned = _pinned_environment_keys(principal, repo_root)` (lines 121-123) when `principal == own_principal` but `own_pubs` is empty — this is an own-principal path that is NOT the new retry path","Plan: 'Only when the principal is the own principal, an own key exists, and that verification returns mismatch, retry ...' — the no-own-key own-principal case is not the retry path","Plan: 'Give _pinned_environment_keys an unrevoked_only parameter used by the own-principal path only' — 'the own-principal path' is ambiguous given there are two (retry path and no-own-key fallthrough)"],"finding":"The plan's revocation-respecting retry is gated on 'an own key exists', but the own-principal fallthrough where NO own key is held in this clone still routes through _pinned_environment_keys (src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:121-123), which returns revoked keys too; the plan does not specify whether unrevoked_only=True applies to that fallthrough.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f46eac80898b1cabe","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 ('_pinned_environment_keys ... unrevoked_only parameter used by the own-principal path only') and src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:117-123","norm_id":"n55ca42bb8592f1fe","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A clone that does not hold the environment's private key verifies an own-principal cert signed under a pinned key that was later revoked — it falls through to the pinned path and, if that path keeps today's revoked-inclusive behaviour, certifies a revoked key"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the own-principal fallthrough p